-- title:
--   Deligne–Serre lifting over a complete DVR, weight two
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \geq 1$ (nonzero) and a set $S$ of natural numbers, and let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, and let $\theta \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ be a ring homomorphism into the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by those weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space. Then there exists a type $\mathcal{O}'$ carrying the structure of a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure making $\mathcal{O}'$ a finite $\mathcal{O}$-module with local and injective structure map $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}'$, and a ring homomorphism $\chi \colon \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}'$ such that for every $t \in \mathbb{T}$ the residue class of $\chi(t)$ in the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$ equals the image of $\theta(t)$ under the induced map of residue fields.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Serre lifting lemma for the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra, stated relative to a coefficient ring: a residual system of Hecke eigenvalues with values in the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ is the reduction of a characteristic-zero eigensystem valued in the ring of integers of a finite extension of the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$, the extension $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}'$ being unavoidable. It is used downstream to produce characteristic-zero Hecke eigensystems with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials, with prescribed behaviour of $U_q$ at primes dividing a squarefree level, and in the ordinarity arguments at the Taylor–Wiles level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_ringHom_heckeAlgebra_residue_eq_map_of_hasIntegralStructure.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_ringHom_heckeAlgebra_residue_eq_map_of_hasIntegralStructure
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (S : Set ℕ)
    {𝒪 : Type} [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪] [Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪)]
    [CharZero 𝒪]
    (θ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S →+* IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪)
    (hint : CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2) :
    ∃ (𝒪' : Type) (_ : CommRing 𝒪') (_ : IsDomain 𝒪') (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪')
      (_ : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪') 𝒪')
      (_ : Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪')) (_ : CharZero 𝒪')
      (_ : Algebra 𝒪 𝒪') (_ : Module.Finite 𝒪 𝒪') (_ : IsLocalHom (algebraMap 𝒪 𝒪')),
    Function.Injective (algebraMap 𝒪 𝒪') ∧
    ∃ χ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S →+* 𝒪',
      ∀ t, IsLocalRing.residue 𝒪' (χ t) = IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap 𝒪 𝒪') (θ t) := by sorry
